    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0650" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2454</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-19T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4176. Sir Edward Grey privately informs me
                    that Spring Rice and Jusserand report that they think the present
                    moment inopportune to present their note, but that on an intimation from you
                    they will present it at any time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
